The section under review is a SQL query-builder (`create_postgres_query`) that constructs a raw SQL string from user-supplied filter values. This is a SQL-injection concern (CWE-89), not an authorization flaw. The authorization-relevant behavior — that `list_dids` scopes results to the caller's `scope`/`vo` — is enforced in the caller (`postgres_meta.py:257-264`), which is outside this section and unchanged. I found no policy text defining an access-control rule for DID metadata queries, and no changed/removed line in this section that omits or weakens an authentication/role/ownership check. The only changed line in `print_query` is a docstring. Therefore there is no candidate authorization flaw in this section.

